      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2011 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "We report on a 20-year-old man who presented with an extensive acute anteroseptal myocardial infarction (from a thrombotic occlusion of the left anterior coronary artery) as the initial manifestation of hereditary protein C deficiency. This case report, along with previous reports, indicates that a diagnosis of protein C deficiency in young patients with myocardial infarctions is essential for more appropriate management and for the prevention of recurrent events. Furthermore, family screening could lead to a prophylactic approach in carriers of this mutation."
      },
